# Extension Coding Conventions

## No File I/O in Extension Host

The extension host must NEVER read file contents directly:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — blocks UI thread, duplicates CLI logic
const content = fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf-8');

// ✅ GOOD — send absolute paths to CLI, it handles I/O
const contextPaths = contextProvider.getAbsolutePaths();
await agentService.chat({ contextPaths, ... });
```

## IPC via CliService

```typescript
// Send a request and await response
const result = await cliService.send({ id: uuid, action: 'ping', payload: {} });

// Subscribe to push events (streaming)
const dispose = cliService.onCliMessage('chat:chunk', (msg) => { ... });
// Remember to dispose when done
```

## Webview ↔ Extension Protocol

Extension → Webview: `ExtensionCommand` (appendChunk, initialize, modeChanged, …)
Webview → Extension: `WebviewCommand` (sendMessage, selectAgent, selectMode, …)

```typescript
// Extension side
this.post({ command: 'modeChanged', payload: { mode: 'agent' } });

// Webview side (main.ts)
postMessage({ command: 'selectMode', payload: { mode: 'agent' } });
```

## Secrets Storage

```typescript
// ✅ Store
await context.secrets.store('toddspect.connectors.copilot.token', token);

// ✅ Read
const token = await context.secrets.get('toddspect.connectors.copilot.token');
```

Never store secrets in VS Code settings (they appear in settings.json in plain text).

## Adding a VS Code Command

1. Register in `extension.ts`: `vscode.commands.registerCommand('toddspect.myCmd', ...)`
2. Declare in `package.json` → `contributes.commands`
3. Add to palette via `contributes.menus` if needed
